From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BicTerm <embed@bicterm.invalid>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:32:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] embed: hide the Local endpoint under HERDR_EMBED_HIDE_LOCAL

behind the bicterm-embed feature, HERDR_EMBED_HIDE_LOCAL=1 hides the
Local endpoint for embedding hosts that run no local herdr server (herd
mode, where the stock Local row would redial a nonexistent socket
forever). The env is parsed once at client boot and carried as
immutable shell policy on ClientShellConfig; the startup Local dial,
Local method registration, and the late Local catalog transition are
skipped; catalog reloads never recreate the Local row; and removing the
active machine selects the first enabled survivor instead of falling
back to Local. With no active machine the Local id stays an internal
no-active sentinel: the unavailable frame reads "No machine selected"
and the new-workspace footer stays disabled. Endpoint chrome (machine
rows, machine parents in navigation, the endpoint sidebar) now applies
whenever any real machine exists, so a sole machine no longer falls
into the legacy local-only renderers. Stock builds keep every path byte
for byte: the exact value "1" is required and the stock const fn
ignores the env entirely.
against 0.9.1 the compose_unavailable local_snapshot shortcut (a sole
endpoint gets the legacy local-only sidebar) now also requires that sole
endpoint to really be Local: with Local hidden it is a machine and must
keep the endpoint sidebar and its machine hits.
